  ('meribel-france', '01F', 'Méribel', 'France', 'The wooded heart of the world''s biggest ski area', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'French Alps', '{"ski","family","romance","ultra","hiking","wellness","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Geographic heart of Les 3 Vallees — world''s largest linked ski area: 600 km slopes + 50 km ski routes, 159 lifts, 1,100-3,230 m, 7 linked resorts","Meribel valley: ~150 km pistes, 76 runs (8 green/36 blue/23 red/9 black), 53 lifts; villages Les Allues 1,100 m to Mottaret 1,750 m; top Mont du Vallon 2,952 m","Central pivot — ski to Courchevel (via La Saulire) AND Val Thorens/Belleville (via Mont de la Chambre) and home the same day; 85% of domain above 1,800 m","Founded by Scot Major Peter Lindsay from 1938 with a wood/stone/slate chalet-only building code — the catered-chalet capital and British-favourite family/apres base","Racing pedigree: 1992 Albertville Olympics (men''s ice hockey + women''s Alpine); 2023 FIS Alpine World Ski Championships women''s races on the Roc de Fer","Luxury layer: Le Coucou (5-star, 55 keys + 2 chalets, ski-in/ski-out at 1,600 m) and L''Helios (5-star, 18 keys + spa)","Domain scale: 340 marked runs, 105 km2 skiable, 53 high-altitude restaurants, 2,700 snow guns; 3V slope mix 336 km easy / 204 km intermediate / 60 km difficult","Best time Dec-Apr (Feb most snow-sure, Mar best conditions); green summer Jun-Sep ~20 C for hiking + biking"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 (EU all-services) / 15 SAMU medical / 17 police / 18 fire; mountain rescue via PGHM (dial 112)","hospital":"In-resort medical centres (Meribel Centre + Mottaret); regional Centre Hospitalier Albertville-Moutiers (CHAM), Moutiers site ~18 km; serious trauma transfer Grenoble/Chambery, often by helicopter","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"High-alpine winter sports: off-piste avalanche risk (Meteo-France Meribel bulle