  ('mosel-valley-germany', '01F', 'The Mosel Valley', 'Germany', 'Steep-slope Riesling, hairpin bends, and a castle on every', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'The Rhine & Mosel', '{"wine","river","culture","romance","hiking"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["World''s largest Riesling-growing area on hand-worked slate slopes — coldest/steepest/most northerly great white-wine country","Cochem + Reichsburg Cochem — turreted neo-Gothic castle (rebuilt from 1868), tour-only ~40 min, ~EUR 5","Bernkastel-Kues — medieval half-timbered Marktplatz + ruined Burg Landshut + the ''Doctor'' vineyard (~3.25 ha, up to ~70% grade)","Bremmer Calmont — Europe''s steepest vineyard (up to 65 degrees, ~380 m) + Calmont Klettersteig via ferrata","Beilstein — the ''Sleeping Beauty of the Mosel'', a preserved medieval wine hamlet under the Metternich ruin","Moselsteig long-distance trail; Gebrueder Kolb day cruises (Cochem/Bernkastel/Traben-Trarbach)","Middle Mosel Wine Festival Bernkastel-Kues ~3-7 Sep 2026 (largest); Trier is the Roman gateway city upstream"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 (fire/ambulance) / 110 (police) / 116 117 (medical on-call)","hospital":"Klinikum Mutterhaus (Trier) main; Cochem + Zell regional clinics for the wine towns","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_codes":["T"],"advisory_note":"active terrorism advisory — public/tourist locations, incl. crowded harvest wine festivals + Christmas markets","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"do NOT drink and drive the wine routes (use driver/shuttle/train/tour); steep loose exposed vineyard paths — Moselsteig + Calmont Klettersteig (up to 65 deg) need sure-footing + head for heights, avoid wet/ice; Mosel cruising low-risk; kayak/SUP = life jacket + cold water + cruise traffic; NO alpine spine","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/germany","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-08-11T10:18:05